{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom at e1c7886db74f1700ef646fd939a719463fb98e59 on request/event-sequence-numbers. Every projected event carries a Sequence: its position in the log, derived from the fold's per-record index and counted from one, so a re-fold gives every reader the same number. ProfileVersion advances to workroom-fold@2 because a resident reusing an older checkpoint would serve zero for every event. Statements and Decisions carry it; the UI reads it in place of its client-side derivation; SKILL.md distinguishes the canonical identifier, which is the only name the fold resolves, from `#N`, which is for saying out loud.","body":{"commit":"e1c7886db74f1700ef646fd939a719463fb98e59","path":"internal/workroom"}}